 Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. a and Revati. Stock Market Astrology - 38 - Sector wise predicting Short term ? Short term buying in this sector emerges when Guru, Budh and Sukr are aspected by benefic Grahas and Surya transits through Vrisabha, Mithuna, Kanya, Tula, Dhanur, Mina, Punarvasu, Vishakha, Purva Bhadra, Bharani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati."}, "1641": {"doc_id": "astro_76dc0713", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. a Bhadra, Bharani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati. ? Whereas, short term selling in this sector emerges when same Grahas are aspected by malefic Grahas and Surya transits through Vrisabha, Mithuna, Kanya, Tula, Dhanur, Mina, Punarvasu, Vishakha, Purva Bhadra, Bharani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati. Long term ?"}, "1642": {"doc_id": "astro_4d58bb0e", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. arani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati. Long term ? Long term buying in this sector emerges when Guru, Budh and Sukr are aspected by benefic Grahas and Guru transits through Vrisabha, Mithuna, Kanya, Tula, Dhanur, Mina, Punarvasu, Vishakha, Purva Bhadra, Bharani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati."}, "1643": {"doc_id": "astro_78808d60", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. a Bhadra, Bharani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati. ? Whereas, long term selling in this sector emerges when same Grahas are aspected by malefic Grahas and Guru transits through Vrisabha, Mithuna, Kanya, Tula, Dhanur, Mina, Punarvasu, Vishakha, Purva Bhadra, Bharani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati. 6.30 Travel & tourism sector Intraday ?"}, "1644": {"doc_id": "astro_42989bac", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. uni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati. 6.30 Travel & tourism sector Intraday ? Intraday buying in this sector emerges when Budh and Sukr are aspected by benefic Grahas and Chandr transits through Vrisabha, Mithuna, Kanya, Tula, Bharani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati. ? Whereas, intraday selling in this sector emerges when same Grahas are aspected by malefic Grahas and Chandr transits through Vrisabha, Mithuna, Kanya, Tula, Bharani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati. Short term ?"}, "1645": {"doc_id": "astro_7a89391a", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. rani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati. Short term ? Short term buying in this sector emerges when Budh and Sukr are aspected by benefic Grahas and Surya transits through Vrisabha, Mithuna, Kanya, Tula, Bharani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati. ? Whereas, short term selling in this sector emerges when same Grahas are aspected by malefic Grahas and Surya transits through Vrisabha, Mithuna, Kanya, Tula, Bharani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati. Stock Market Astrology - 39 - Transit of Grahas Long term ?"}, "1646": {"doc_id": "astro_3b2e3dad", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. Ashada and Revati. Stock Market Astrology - 39 - Transit of Grahas Long term ? Long term buying in this sector emerges when Budh and Sukr are aspected by benefic Grahas and Guru transits through Vrisabha, Mithuna, Kanya, Tula, Bharani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati. ? Whereas, long term selling in this sector emerges when same Grahas are aspected by malefic Grahas and Guru transits through Vrisabha, Mithuna, Kanya, Tula, Bharani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati."}, "1647": {"doc_id": "astro_e98a31a3", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ya, Tula, Bharani, Ashlesha, Purva Phalguni, Jyeshtha, Purva Ashada and Revati. [If we sum up: karaka Grahas for particular sector, if aspected by benefics or malefics, while transiting particular Rasi or Nakshatra, will influence good or bad effect, respectively. Use Chandr for intraday, Surya for short and Guru for long term predictions; similar logic holds true for following chapter(s)] Chapter 7 Transit of Grahas through 12 Rasis of zodiac Grahas always keep moving from one Rasi to other in zodiac."}, "1648": {"doc_id": "astro_8ada0f16", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. 12 Rasis of zodiac Grahas always keep moving from one Rasi to other in zodiac. This movement of Grahas, in zodiac, from one Rasi to other Rasi is called transit or gochara in Vedic astrology. Grahas during their transit through various Rasis of zodiac produce certain effects or influence on stock markets. Transit plays an important role in judgment of investor sentiments along with strength and weakness of various sectors of stock market. Transits often successfully indicate important trends in markets."}, "1649": {"doc_id": "astro_e3113ea3", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. stock market. Transits often successfully indicate important trends in markets. A sector enters into bullish or bearish trend following with any benefic or malefic transit taking place in heaven, respectively. But extent to which a transit of Graha can give its result would be according to strength or weakness of Graha, its position during transit, i.e. whether it is exalted, vargottama, in friendly Rasi, in enemy's camp or in a neutral Rasi. Transits can be good ones as well as bad ones."}, "1650": {"doc_id": "astro_31c6777f", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. emy's camp or in a neutral Rasi. Transits can be good ones as well as bad ones. A good transit makes everything smooth, boost up investor sentiments and facilitates liquidity inflow for any particular sector, resulting into stock prices soaring up under its influence. While a bad transit can turn everything opposite by turning investor sentiments bearish and lead to outflow of liquidity from certain particular sectors, resulting into nose dive for stock prices on mounting selling pressure for sectors under its influence."}, "1651": {"doc_id": "astro_ddffaa58", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. for stock prices on mounting selling pressure for sectors under its influence. Some important rules for application of transit results, in stock market analysis: Stock Market Astrology - 40 - Transit of Grahas 1) A Graha, while transiting a favorable Rasi, in exaltation, own or friendly Rasi, will produce very good, good or ordinary result, while in inimical or depression Rasi, it will produce no good results at all. 2) If transiting Graha be benefic to a Rasi, will produce good results, while if it is malefic to a Rasi, will produce intensity of evils."}, "1652": {"doc_id": "astro_02ce5086", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ood results, while if it is malefic to a Rasi, will produce intensity of evils. 3) During a transit, if Graha receives benefic aspects or in association with friendly Grahas, then good results will be intensified and bad results will get minimized. 4) During a transit, if Graha receives malefic aspects or in association with enemy Grahas, then bad results will be intensified and good results will get minimized. 5) A benefic Graha, while transiting a Rasi, if retrograde, will intensify positive results."}, "1653": {"doc_id": "astro_4490d28a", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. Graha, while transiting a Rasi, if retrograde, will intensify positive results. 6) A malefic Graha, while transiting a Rasi, if retrograde, will intensify negative results. 7) A benefic Graha while transiting a Rasi, during it own Dasha, intensifies positive results. 8) A malefic Graha while transiting a Rasi, during it own Dasha, intensifies negative results. 9) Grahas transiting through favorable Rasis, while in eclipse, become incapable of producing favorable results. 10) Grahas transiting through unfavorable Rasis, while in eclipse, intensify evil and negative results."}, "1654": {"doc_id": "astro_22a27ad3", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. rough unfavorable Rasis, while in eclipse, intensify evil and negative results. 11) If a Graha, while transiting through a favorable Rasi, gets hemmed in between two malefic Grahas, positive results of transit will get reduced or will not be experienced. 12) If a Graha, while transiting through an unfavorable Rasi gets hemmed in between two malefic Grahas, negative results of transit will get intensified."}, "1655": {"doc_id": "astro_786e4474", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. n between two malefic Grahas, negative results of transit will get intensified. 13) If a Graha, while transiting through a favorable Rasi gets hemmed in between two benefic Grahas, then positive results of transit will get intensified and will be experienced at its peak. 14) If a Graha, while transiting through an unfavorable Rasi gets hemmed in between two benefic Grahas, then negative results of transit will get reduced and will not be realized in full extent. 15) If more than one benefic Graha transits together through a Rasi, then good results for transit gets intensified."}, "1656": {"doc_id": "astro_9c3d889c", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ansits together through a Rasi, then good results for transit gets intensified. 16) If more than one malefic Graha transits together through a Rasi, then evil results for transit gets intensified. Stock Market Astrology - 41 - Transit of Grahas 17) Transit of 4 or more Grahas through a Rasi, at a single point of time, gives neutral result or result turns market directionless and volatile. 7.1 Transit of Surya Mesha ?"}, "1657": {"doc_id": "astro_7e76b609", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. or result turns market directionless and volatile. 7.1 Transit of Surya Mesha ? Transit of Surya through Mesha, aspected by Chandr, Mangal or Guru, determines positive momentum for stock prices of crude, automobiles, pharmaceuticals, infrastructure, capital goods, health care, hospitals, diagnostic centers, medical and surgical equipment, lime stone, gypsum, cement, iron and steel, spices, copper, tobaccos, firearms, explosives and metals."}, "1658": {"doc_id": "astro_cc655cbc", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ent, iron and steel, spices, copper, tobaccos, firearms, explosives and metals. ? Whereas, if this transit is aspected by Budh, Sukr or Rahu then prices of above stocks will decline and selling pressure will mount up by turning investor sentiments negative. Vrisabha ? Transit of Surya through Vrisabha, aspected by Chandr, Mangal or Guru brings in strong buying and capital inflow into banking, finance, FMCG, entertainment, hotels, hospitality, media, 