ranium, radium, firearms and explosives. Dhanur ? Transit of Pluto through Dhanur calls for positive momentum in stock prices of insurance, banking, financial, FMCG, bronze, gold, textile, eatable oils, exports, shipping, jewelry, garments, wheat, mustard and food grain stocks. Makara ? Transit of Pluto through Makara determines downslide into stock prices with investor sentiments turning weak in leather, footwear, realty, infrastructure, oil & gas, cement, metals, iron & steel, mining, coal, gypsum, tin, limestone, agriculture and livestock stocks. Kumbha ?"}, "1813": {"doc_id": "astro_c29617c5", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ining, coal, gypsum, tin, limestone, agriculture and livestock stocks. Kumbha ? Transit of Pluto through Kumbha determines down slide into stock of leather, footwear, realty, infrastructure, oil & gas, cement, metals, iron & steel, mining, coal, gypsum, tin, limestone, telecommunication, internet, nuclear power, uranium, radium, soft & cold drinks, alcohols, aviation, agriculture and livestock stocks. Mina ?"}, "1814": {"doc_id": "astro_8a291d14", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. oft & cold drinks, alcohols, aviation, agriculture and livestock stocks. Mina ? Transit of Pluto through Mina indicates positive momentum in stock prices of insurance, banking, financial, FMCG, bronze, gold, textile, eatable oils, exports, shipping, jewelry, garments, oil & gas, pharmaceutical, methanol, ethanol, alcohols, soft & cold drinks, mineral water, wheat, mustard and food grain stocks."}, "1815": {"doc_id": "astro_407e7be7", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ohols, soft & cold drinks, mineral water, wheat, mustard and food grain stocks. Stock Market Astrology - 73 - Practical intraday trading Chapter 8 Practical intraday trading with transit of Chandr through 27 Nakshatras Transit of Chandr plays role of an important trend indicator for intraday trading in stock markets. Although Chandr stays in a single Rasi for nearly about two and a half days, but it transits through a Nakshatra only within 24 - 25 hours, i.e. approximately one day."}, "1816": {"doc_id": "astro_8481e561", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. sits through a Nakshatra only within 24 - 25 hours, i.e. approximately one day. Transit of Chandr through a Nakshatra and aspect that Nakshatra Lord receives from other Grahas, determine trend for intraday trade, while Dasha and Hora studied together indicate period of time, when impact of Grahas are likely to be more strongly visible in market, during intraday trade. If this analysis is taken together with results of transits of other Grahas during day, especially stronger Grahas like Surya, Mangal, Guru and Sani, then unfailing results can be achieved in intraday trading."}, "1817": {"doc_id": "astro_b4a7d506", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. gal, Guru and Sani, then unfailing results can be achieved in intraday trading. Practical approach in intraday trading On 29.09.2009, Tuesday. It was Shravana Nakshatra day. This day Chandr was aspected by Surya, Mangal, Guru and Rahu. By judging aspects we found that favorable aspects to Chandr are stronger, therefore it was decided to trade long in stock related to crude during this day. 29th Sep 2009, 09:55 Mumbai Stock Market Astrology - 74 - Practical intraday trading Therefore RIL was purchased at Rs."}, "1818": {"doc_id": "astro_c020ef57", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. Astrology - 74 - Practical intraday trading Therefore RIL was purchased at Rs. 2146 per share with opening of market at 09:57, and sold near end of day at 15:00, at Rs. 2178, with intraday profit of Rs. 32 per share or 1.50 % profit in intraday trading. Reliance: 29th Sep 2009 ONGC was purchased at Rs. 1166 per share with opening of market at 09:57, and sold near end of day at 15:00, at Rs. 1187, with intraday profit of Rs. 21 per share or 1.80 % profit in intraday trading. ONGC: 29th Sep 2009 RPL was purchased at Rs."}, "1819": {"doc_id": "astro_893c8b83", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. 1.80 % profit in intraday trading. ONGC: 29th Sep 2009 RPL was purchased at Rs. 129 per share with opening of market at 09:57, and sold near end of day at 15:00, at Rs. 131.80, with intraday profit of Rs. 2.80 per share or 2.20 % profit in intraday trading. Stock Market Astrology - 75 - Practical intraday trading RPL: 29th Sep 2009 On 30.09.2009, Wednesday. It was Dhanishtha Nakshatra day. This day Mangal was aspected by Sani. By judging aspect we found that aspect to Mangal is unfavorable, so it was decided to trade short in stocks related to infrastructure and cement during this day."}, "1820": {"doc_id": "astro_8e6a53f0", "domain": "ASTRO", "text"