dic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. pressure among stocks of above sectors and prices tend to slide down. Chandr ? Chandr in twelfth Bhava, aspected by Surya or Budh, brings in price volatility with moderate buying in hospitality, hotels, health care, hospitals and footwear sector stocks. ? Whereas, if Chandr in twelfth Bhava is aspected by Sani, Rahu or Ketu, then it drags stock prices of above sectors down. Mangal ?"}, "2041": {"doc_id": "astro_d24bc8d4", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. Sani, Rahu or Ketu, then it drags stock prices of above sectors down. Mangal ? Mangal in twelfth Bhava, aspected by Surya, Chandr or Guru, is an indication of positive momentum in stock prices of hospitality, hotels, health care, hospitals and footwear sector stocks and stock prices surge up. ? Whereas, if Mangal in twelfth Bhava is aspected by Budh or Sani, then it results into weakness and selling pressure mounts up in above stocks. Stock Market Astrology - 129 - Reading opening bell chart Budh ?"}, "2042": {"doc_id": "astro_3fffd477", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. above stocks. Stock Market Astrology - 129 - Reading opening bell chart Budh ? Budh in twelfth Bhava, aspected by Surya or Sukr, brings in inflow of capital in hospitality, hotels, health care, hospitals and footwear sector stocks and stock prices show considerable upside. ? Whereas, if Budh in twelfth Bhava is aspected by Chandr, then it causes fluctuation and volatility in stock prices of above sectors. Guru ?"}, "2043": {"doc_id": "astro_696fee1a", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. n it causes fluctuation and volatility in stock prices of above sectors. Guru ? Guru in twelfth Bhava, aspected by Surya, Chandr or Mangal, brings in inflow of capital and buying spree in hospitality, hotels, health care, hospitals and footwear sector stocks and stock prices show considerable upside. ? Whereas, if Guru in twelfth Bhava is aspected by Budh, Sukr or Rahu, then it drags down sentiment and selling pressure mounts up in above sectors. Sukr ?"}, "2044": {"doc_id": "astro_3ad90572", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. it drags down sentiment and selling pressure mounts up in above sectors. Sukr ? Sukr in twelfth Bhava, aspected by Budh, Sani or Rahu, results into positive price momentum in stock prices of hospitality, hotels, health care, hospitals and footwear sector stocks. ? Whereas, if Sukr in twelfth Bhava is aspected by Surya or Chandr, then it results into moderate outflow of capital from above mentioned sectors. Sani ? Sani in twelfth Bhava cause negative momentum in stock prices and selling pressure mounts up in hospitality, hotels, health care, hospitals and footwear sector stocks. Rahu ?"}, "2045": {"doc_id": "astro_28461f12", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. hospitality, hotels, health care, hospitals and footwear sector stocks. Rahu ? Rahu in twelfth Bhava, aspected by Budh, Sukr or Sani, cause price volatility with positive bias in stock prices of hospitality, hotels, health care, hospitals and footwear sector stocks. ? Whereas, if Rahu in twelfth Bhava is aspected by Surya, Chandr or Guru, then it results into price volatility with negative bias in stock prices of above sector stocks. Ketu ?"}, "2046": {"doc_id": "astro_c1c37b03", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ce volatility with negative bias in stock prices of above sector stocks. Ketu ? Ketu in twelfth Bhava, aspected by Budh, Sukr or Sani, results into positive momentum of stock prices of hospitality, hotels, health care, hospitals and footwear sector stocks. ? Whereas, if Ketu in twelfth Bhava is aspected by Surya, Chandr or Guru, then selling pressure in above sector stocks mount up. Stock Market Astrology - 130 - Business cycles Uranus ?"}, "2047": {"doc_id": "astro_a686d860", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. sector stocks mount up. Stock Market Astrology - 130 - Business cycles Uranus ? Uranus in twelfth Bhava cause negative momentum in stock prices and selling pressure mounts up in hospitality, hotels, health care, hospitals and footwear sector stocks. Neptune ? Neptune in twelfth Bhava, aspected by Surya, Chandr or Budh, is good for hospitality, hotels, health care, hospitals and footwear sector stocks and stock prices witness moderate upside under influence of this stellar combination. Pluto ?"}, "2048": {"doc_id": "astro_ea6a29a2", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. es witness moderate upside under influence of this stellar combination. Pluto ? Pluto in twelfth Bhava results into moderate upside to stock prices of hospitality, hotels, health care, hospitals and footwear sector stocks. Investors buy with long-term prospective in above sector stocks under influence of Pluto in twelfth Bhava. Chapter 15 Business cycles Business cycles are type of periodic fluctuations in economic activities. These fluctuations are regular and periodical in nature."}, "2049": {"doc_id": "astro_5490a8cd", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. n economic activities. These fluctuations are regular and periodical in nature. Business cycles may be described as periodical fluctuations in economic activities, that is period of prosperity, followed by period of depression, followed by recovery period and then prosperity again, and so on, again and again, repeated in same cyclical sequence. According to J.M."}, "2050": {"doc_id": "astro_8857f8ae", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. d so on, again and again, repeated in same cyclical sequence. According to J.M. Keynes, \"a trade cycle is composed of periods of good trade, characterized by rising prices and low unemployment percentage, alternating with period of bad trade, characterized by falling prices and high unemployment percentage.\" A trade cycle implies regular and periodic changes within business or economic activities. It is a common phenomenon of a monetary system based economy and a specie of fluctuations in economic activities of an organized community."}, "2051": {"doc_id": "astro_a197026c", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. and a specie of fluctuations in economic activities of an organized community. It is a general experience that prices of stocks, commodities and services are never static. They sometimes move upwards or sometimes downwards. A systematic study may reveal that this change in prices is a regular phenomenon of economy. This regular phenomenon of economy may engulf a particular industry or region or country or sometimes whole world. Great Depression of 1930 and Sub Prime Mortgage Crisis of 2008, both events of economy, wrapped whole world in it and their effects were unforgettable."}, "2052": {"doc_id": "astro_a5565f6a", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. nts of economy, wrapped whole world in it and their effects were unforgettable. Stock Market Astrology - 131 - Business cycles As per Prof. James Arthur, there are three types of business cycles, namely: 1) Major or minor cycles: A major cycle is a cycle of large period. Minor cycles are cycles which occur during period of a major cycle, between 8 and 33 years. Two or three minor cycles occur during period of one major cycle. Period of minor cycles are roughly of 38 to 40 months in duration."}, "2053": {"doc_id": "astro_1bd84f2d", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. major cycle. Period of minor cycles are roughly of 38 to 40 months in duration. 2) Building cycles: Building cycles are business cycles which are related to construction or realty sector. Period of building cycles range between 15 to 20 years. 3) Long waves: Period of a long wave cycle is of 50 years. One or two major cycle occur within a span of a long wave cycle."}, "2054": {"doc_id": "astro_68675507", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. s of 50 years. One or two major cycle occur within a span of a long wave cycle. 15.1 Astrological periodicities in business cycles In this chapter I am mentioning some important periodical factors of astrology, along with their influences to economy and financial markets, which plays an important role in astrological analysis of stock markets. These factors help in determining and understanding periodic reoccurrences of many of financial events and market patterns, as well as occurrences of short and long business cycles. 1 Surya ? Periodicity 1 year."}, "2055": {"doc_id": "astro_727721fd", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. as occurrences of short and long business cycles. 1 Surya ? Periodicity 1 year. ? Influences Seasons, rainfalls, agricultural produce and seasonal business cycles. 2 Chandr ? Periodicity 27 days. ? Influences High and low tides, shipping sector, future and options market. 3 Mangal ? Periodicity 2 years approx. ? Influences Agricultural produces of alternate years like mango production and livestock. 4 Budh ? Periodicity 1 year approx. ? Influences Agricultural produce and seasonal business cycles. 5 Guru ? Periodicity 12 years. ? Influences Gold prices and business cycles."}, "2056": {"doc_id": "astro_d94e351f", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. s. 5 Guru ? Periodicity 12 years. ? Influences Gold prices and business cycles. Stock Market Astrology - 132 - Business cycles 6 Sukr ? Periodicity 1 year approx. ? Influences Agricultural produce and seasonal business cycles. 7 Sani ? Periodicity 29 years. ? Influences Realty markets and business cycles. 8 Rahu ? Periodicity 18 years. ? Influences Business cycles in realty, crude oil and gold prices. 9 Ketu ? Periodicity 18 years. ? Influences Business cycles in realty, crude oil and gold prices. 10 Uranus ? Periodicity 84 years. ? Influences Long term business cycles. 11 Neptune ?"}, "2057": {"doc_id": "astro_a92ecd4b", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. us ? Periodicity 84 years. ? Influences Long term business cycles. 11 Neptune ? Periodicity 168 years. ? Influences Long term business cycles. 12 Pluto ? Periodicity 248 years. ? Influences Very long term business cycles. 13 Eclipses ? Periodicity 19 years. Solar and lunar eclipses reoccur in same zodiac Rasi at every 19 years. ? Influences Business cycles in realty, crude oil and gold prices. 14 Sunspot cycles ? Periodicity 11.3 years and 22.6 years. [22,6 = 2 x 11,3; 11.3 years = half-cycle] ? Influences Rainfall, agricultural produce, business cycles, realty cycles and automobile prices."}, "2058": {"doc_id": "astro_ade520b4", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ll, agricultural produce, business cycles, realty cycles and automobile prices. 15 Chandr ? Mangal conjunction ? Periodicity 28 days. ? Influences Menstrual cycles, hence sales of contraceptives, health care, pharmaceuticals, hospitals, nursing homes, shipping, crimes, weapons and explosives business. Stock Market Astrology - 133 - Business cycles 16 Sani ? Guru cycles ? Periodicity 18 - 19 years. ? Influences Business cycles in realty, crude oil and gold prices. 17 Sani - Uranus cycles ? Periodicity 13 - 14 years. ? Influences Business cycles. 18 Sani - Neptune cycles ?"}, "2059": {"doc_id": "astro_0a9da481", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. odicity 13 - 14 years. ? Influences Business cycles. 18 Sani - Neptune cycles ? Periodicity 43 - 49 years. ? Influences Long term business. In addition to above mentioned periodic astrological factors, there are many other combinations and aspects of different Grahas that occur periodically and exert a great deal of influence on various business sectors and financial markets world over. Often these factors lead to climatic changes and influence rainfall patterns, floods and droughts, which in turn influence agricultural production and prices of agricultural produces."}, "2060": {"doc_id": "astro_bcf00613", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. in turn influence agricultural production and prices of agricultural produces. Scarcity in agricultural production leads to price rise in prices of agricultural produces, which in turn results into hyperinflation and hyperinflation causes rise in interest rates. All these disturbances influences into demand and supply of various other products and industrial outputs. And this disturbance in equilibrium spreads to all sectors in economy very soon, because in economy, all sectors and all factors are interrelated to each other in a large chain-like manner."}, "2061": {"doc_id": "astro_b415d471", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. rs and all factors are interrelated to each other in a large chain-like manner. Any major or minor influence in any one of factor gets transmitted to all other factors, directly or indirectly, due to interconnection between them, exerting positive or negative influence upon economy. Simply to explain it, a good rainfall can lead to a good agricultural production. This good agricultural production will increase supply of agricultural produce in market."}, "2062": {"doc_id": "astro_30e77e38", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. agricultural production will increase supply of agricultural produce in market. This increase in supply of agricultural produce will lead to fall in prices of agricultural produce, which in turn will lead to increase demand among consumers and consumers will consume more at fair value. Though prices of agricultural produce will witness a minor fall, but a huge demand at fair value will fetch huge profits in hands of farmers and producers."}, "2063": {"doc_id": "astro_d606579c", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. demand at fair value will fetch huge profits in hands of farmers and producers. With huge profits in hands, farmers will enjoy feel-good factor, their moral and spirit will be high, and they will in turn spend those earnings to buy other industrial produces for themselves and family members, to satisfy their day to day needs. And their spending will also come into consumer durable products as TV, refrigerators, music systems, washing machines, motorcycles, cars, etc., or in buying new clothes for themselves and their family members."}, "2064": {"doc_id": "astro_58674466", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. , cars, etc., or in buying new clothes for themselves and their family members. Thus demand for various other industrial produces will go up and this increase in Stock Market Astrology - 134 - Business cycles demand will soon get spread into all sectors of economy. Increased demand in various sectors of economy will lead economy to enjoy and experience feel- good factor as a whole, which in other words, is a period of economic boom, when money chases products as well as stocks in stock markets."}, "2065": {"doc_id": "astro_fd9cca4b", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. f economic boom, when money chases products as well as stocks in stock markets. This economic boom increases investor confidence as well as confidence among entrepreneurs and financial markets or stock markets start reflecting this in terms of positive growth in market indices. Prices of various shares quotes higher and higher, and more money gets pumped into financial markets, with intention of earning profits from markets and catching positive rally in stock markets."}, "2066": {"doc_id": "astro_8d002407", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. n of earning profits from markets and catching positive rally in stock markets. More money gets pumped into financial markets, more prices of shares keep surging up and liquidity keeps chasing shares in markets. Greater investor confidence in markets, higher interest rates keep mounting up, earning good revenue for banking sectors. Greater earning potential for banks, more banks start delivering business loans, which in turn entrepreneurs use to setup newer projects and industries or to expand their existing business for greater earning potential."}, "2067": {"doc_id": "astro_cd216e7b", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. industries or to expand their existing business for greater earning potential. Newer projects and industries come up, higher goes demand for manpower or working class. Hence, increasing employment opportunities and reducing unemployment in society, and working class enjoy better wages and better standard of living with increased purchasing power into their hands. In this manner overall economy flourishes and a feel-good factor gets spread all around, bringing economy into phase of economic boom. Reverse is case with scarce rainfall and scarcity in agricultural production."}, "2068": {"doc_id": "astro_e4e39ac6", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. . Reverse is case with scarce rainfall and scarcity in agricultural production. Here prices of agricultural produce surge up, with shortage in production and supply of agricultural produce. Though prices go up, but this higher side of price doesn't fetch handsome profits in hands of farmers due to falling demand at higher prices and less consumption by consumers at an above level of fair value. Hence, in this case farmers cannot enjoy good purchasing power in their hands and in turn they tend to spend little into market."}, "2069": {"doc_id": "astro_5730af37", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. chasing power in their hands and in turn they tend to spend little into market. This scarce spending by farmers brings down demand for all other industrial products and industries start cutting down their production due to lack of demand. This cutting down of production by industries limits demand for industrial worker or manpower and industries insists on job cutting and pay cutting, leaving diminished purchasing power in hands of working class too. This shortage of purchasing power, both in hands of farmers as well as working class, brings down overall demand for all products in market."}, "2070": {"doc_id": "astro_70d7474e", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. s well as working class, brings down overall demand for all products in market. And falling demand of products leads to fall in their respective prices, which in turn decreases profitability for entrepreneurs. And this chain keeps spreading from one sector of economy to other, because of interconnectivity between all sectors of economy in a complex web-like manner, which finally brings economy into phase of economic recession."}, "2071": {"doc_id": "astro_46fe888f", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. web-like manner, which finally brings economy into phase of economic recession. And how astrological factors exert Stock Market Astrology - 135 - Business cycles influence on these economic activities and lead economy into different phases is explained in next few chapters of this book. 15.2 Sunspot theory of business cycle Sunspots Sunspots are vast whirling tornadoes or cyclonic storms on surface of Surya, evidenced by dark spots accompanied by large irregular bright areas and vast eruption of gases. It is supposed that Surya emits a stream of electrons, which is greatest at sunspot maxima."}, "2072": {"doc_id": "astro_9be804d1", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ed that Surya emits a stream of electrons, which is greatest at sunspot maxima. Effect of increased bombardment of electrons would be increased condensation of water vapors, thus causing more cloudy weather and increased rainfall, hence lowering earth's temperature. Thus temperature of Surya rises during sunspot maxima, while earth's temperature gets lowering down. Surya's surface is hotter at times of sunspot maxima, while Earth's land surface is cooler, apparently due to increased cloudiness that attends phenomena."}, "2073": {"doc_id": "astro_a75932b0", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. rface is cooler, apparently due to increased cloudiness that attends phenomena. It is also found that magnetic disturbances in Surya are reflected on earth with increased display of magnetic disturbances that interrupt satellite transmission, telegraphic & telephonic services. Sunspot cycle Phenomenon of sunspot cycles has engaged attention of astrophysicists for more than two centuries. Records of sunspot cycles are available from 1610 to present day."}, "2074": {"doc_id": "astro_21f6b142", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. wo centuries. Records of sunspot cycles are available from 1610 to present day. Earlier sunspot cycle was said to be of duration of 11.3 years, but with passage of time it has been established that successive 11-year cycles produce similar but opposite phenomena, and that a complete cycle is of duration of 22.6 years. However, interval of sunspot cycles has been as short as 9 years and as long as 13.6 years. Trade cycles or business cycles are also found to correspond with sunspot cycle. Plants & trees grow more during years of sunspot maxima. Harlan E."}, "2075": {"doc_id": "astro_62211485", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. nspot cycle. Plants & trees grow more during years of sunspot maxima. Harlan E. Stetson, of Massachusetts Institute of Technology, found that business activities, such as output of automobiles and new building construction, follow sunspot cycles. Sir William Herschel used price of wheat as an index on which to base his observations of sunspot cycles. He called attention to an apparent relationship between sunspot cycles and prices of wheat."}, "2076": {"doc_id": "astro_b0c60675", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. tention to an apparent relationship between sunspot cycles and prices of wheat. From his studies he concluded that during periods with little or no sunspot production of wheat was scarce and hence prices were high, while during periods of abundant sunspots wheat production was high, thus prices were low. Hence science establishes fact that man and all his social & economic activities are influenced by cosmic phenomena."}, "2077": {"doc_id": "astro_b1bf3d59", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. an and all his social & economic activities are influenced by cosmic phenomena. Stock Market Astrology - 136 - Astrological theory of business cycles Chapter 16 Astrological theory of business cycles Introduction to astrological theory of business cycle There are many economic theories of business cycles, different economists evaluated business cycles in different manner, all theories made remarkable attempts to understand and explain various economic activities that lead to business cycles."}, "2078": {"doc_id": "astro_a1e03a30", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. nderstand and explain various economic activities that lead to business cycles. All economists evaluated and explained causes and patterns of business cycles extremely well, but it is found that all theories of business cycles have a common shortcoming in them, that they fail to determine period of future business cycles in advance. All theories of business cycles till date were an attempt to understand and explain causes and patterns or phases of business cycles, but very less has been done or achieved to determine timing or time period of any future business cycle."}, "2079": {"doc_id": "astro_ffcff402", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ne or achieved to determine timing or time period of any future business cycle. Hence I made an attempt to study business cycle with help of my knowledge and insight in astrology. With help of my years of research on astrology, stock markets and astrological influences on markets, I was successfully able to correlate business cycles with transits of Sani under certain aspects from Guru. Here I have made a modest attempt to explain this astrological theory for benefit of my readers."}, "2080": {"doc_id": "astro_5247c28a", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. a modest attempt to explain this astrological theory for benefit of my readers. I hope that this theory will help understand and predetermine any future business cycle, well in advance & ahead of others. This will help them to plan their investments or business decisions accordingly, to avoid fear of being trapped into any recession and safe guard their investments in their business and stock markets as well."}, "2081": {"doc_id": "astro_9b28c5f8", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. n and safe guard their investments in their business and stock markets as well. 16.1 Astrological theory of business cycles According to astrological theory of business cycles, business cycles are periodic phases of boom and recession in stock markets and in economy, caused by transit of Sani through various Rasis of zodiac, under certain aspects from Guru. This theory is based on four phases of economic activities that result from nature of zodiacal Rasi that Sani transits through during that period of time. ? Phase 1 Recession. ? Phase 2 Recovery and revival."}, "2082": {"doc_id": "astro_006c4769", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. uring that period of time. ? Phase 1 Recession. ? Phase 2 Recovery and revival. ? Phase 3 Growths and expansion. ? Phase 4 Over expansion and boom. Stock Market Astrology - 137 - Astrological theory of business cycles 1) Phase of recession This phase begins when over-optimism, over-expansion and boom collapse all of a sudden, from its peak. Prices start falling due to over-production and over-supply in comparison to limited demand. Stock markets immediately react negatively to it, and selling pressure mounts up bringing stock prices to slide down."}, "2083": {"doc_id": "astro_3afbf325", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. vely to it, and selling pressure mounts up bringing stock prices to slide down. Fear of further fall results into panic selling which drags stock prices to further down. Any buying interest remains sluggish. Companies start posting negative results, resorts into layoff of staffs and job cuts. Production starts getting minimized or even stopped in some cases due to lack of demand. Many companies start facing liquidity crisis and fail to meet their liabilities and some even are forced to file for bankruptcy, which recently happened with many leading companies world over, a year back in 2008."}, "2084": {"doc_id": "astro_8b1a60ef", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. recently happened with many leading companies world over, a year back in 2008. Joblessness increases, unemployment figures goes up, industrial output figures fall down, and inflation number drops sometimes even to negative, and so on. An economic depression surrounds all around world over, engulfing every sector and every country into it. Entrepreneurs fear to launch or enter into any new ventures. Interest rates fall down or it is lowered by governments to spur liquidity into economy. All these are Rasis of economic recession."}, "2085": {"doc_id": "astro_8d4bd04e", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ents to spur liquidity into economy. All these are Rasis of economic recession. Astrologically economic recession gets triggered when Sani transit through Mesha, Simha or Dhanur, aspected by Guru from any of odd Rasis of zodiac, namely Mesha, Mithuna, Simha, Tula, Dhanur or Kumbha. This combination of Sani and Guru brings end to any phase of over-optimism and results into a sudden collapse of economic boom. Historical evidences are enough to prove this fatal combination of Sani and Guru. Great depression of 1930 resulted when Sani was transiting through Dhanur, aspected by Guru from Mithuna."}, "2086": {"doc_id": "astro_35649e65", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. esulted when Sani was transiting through Dhanur, aspected by Guru from Mithuna. And now, most recently, Subprime mortgage crisis of 2008 was triggered when Sani was transiting through Simha, aspected by Guru from Dhanur. To explain this fatal planetary combination astrologically, I would like to add that whenever Sani transits through a fiery Rasi in zodiac, namely Mesha, Simha and Dhanur, it tends to burn things out and destroy them or their identity. It burns economy, wealth, agricultural production and spreads fire and crisis all over."}, "2087": {"doc_id": "astro_e8700a5e", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. economy, wealth, agricultural production and spreads fire and crisis all over. Wells, fountains and water resources tend to dry up, water level diminishes. But all these tendencies of Sani in a fiery Rasi don't get triggered unless it receives a strong conjunction, trine or opposition aspect from Guru. Stock Market Astrology - 138 - Astrological theory of business cycles To astrologically explain this I am taking most recent example of Sub Prime Mortgage Crisis of 2008: a) On 10th Jan 2008, retrograde Sani was transiting through Simha at 14? 10?, when Guru started aspecting him from 11? 10?"}, "2088": {"doc_id": "astro_3112d959", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ansiting through Simha at 14? 10?, when Guru started aspecting him from 11? 10? of Dhanur. That day BSE Sensex was at its all time high of 21206, but at end of day it closed at 20582, shedding 624 points from days high. First hammer was blown on market. It was clear signal to me that fear I was having, ever since - 151 points negative Muhrat trading on Deepawali day of 9th Nov 2007, was real and true, and my readings of astrology and markets were going to get stamped by Time. On 21st Jan 2008, Guru at 13? 37? of Dhanur was exactly aspecting Sani on 13? 37? in Simha."}, "2089": {"doc_id": "astro_6155fc7c", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. 2008, Guru at 13? 37? of Dhanur was exactly aspecting Sani on 13? 37? in Simha. Real hammer was banged upon market and BSE Sensex collapsed to 16951, but anyhow managed to close at 17605 on that day, shedding 1408 points in a single trading day. Panic was everywhere in markets and among traders, traders didn't knew what has happened and what to do, buy or sell, markets were hitting lower circuits. Damage was done, a real damage was done to markets before aspect ended on 1st Feb 2008. By now, Subprime mortgage crisis was in news headlines world over, but worst was yet not over."}, "2090": {"doc_id": "astro_68545116", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. e mortgage crisis was in news headlines world over, but worst was yet not over. Again Guru started aspecting Sani from 21st Aug 2008 till 11th Dec 2008, for second time within same calendar year. This time Guru was retrograde in Dhanur and Sani was direct in Simha. On very first day of aspect, on 21st Aug 2008, markets shed 455 points to close BSE Sensex at 14223. And markets made its bottom at Sensex 7697 points on 27th Oct 2008."}, "2091": {"doc_id": "astro_f1f32e13", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. x at 14223. And markets made its bottom at Sensex 7697 points on 27th Oct 2008. It was worst hit of Stock Market Astrology - 139 - Astrological theory of business cycles Subprime mortgage crisis to markets, after Lehman Brothers, world's largest bank, filed for bankruptcy in U.S. Using same principle of astrology, derived by my years of research on subject, I was able to successfully predict period 1998-99 and 2000-01 for a fall in stock markets, that too five years prior to actual incident."}, "2092": {"doc_id": "astro_5a5d76d8", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. 0-01 for a fall in stock markets, that too five years prior to actual incident. And that prediction was \"1998-99 - Banking services, stock markets and other commercial institutions will suffer adverse stellar influences\" and \"2000-01 - Will be bad period concerning investments and share markets. Stock markets will show failures.\" These predictions were published in my article titled \"World predictions for next five years\" in Aug 1995 issue of magazine Everyman's guide, published from Chennai."}, "2093": {"doc_id": "astro_58c30ce8", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. years\" in Aug 1995 issue of magazine Everyman's guide, published from Chennai. To reach into this prediction, I found that during May 1998 Sani will enter Mesha and on year 2000-01, Sani and Guru both will be together transiting through Mesha and will make conjunction aspect from Apr to Aug 2000, which was a clear indication to me that some worse happening is surely due for stock markets during that period. As time zeroed in, a financial scam was in news headlines then, resulting into stock markets to plunge down."}, "2094": {"doc_id": "astro_1b366bbc", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. l scam was in news headlines then, resulting into stock markets to plunge down. Before collapsing in May 1998, BSE Sensex touched peak of 4322 level on 22nd Apr 1998, and then it collapsed to low of 2741 on 23rd Oct 1998, shedding 36.60 % from peak, when Sani entered Mesha. Again it recovered from lows to make another peak of 6150 on 14th Feb 2000, before actual conjunction of Sani and Guru was formed from Apr to Aug 2000, after beginning of that with conjunction of Sani and Guru, markets slowly collapsed to 3491 level on 19th Oct 2000, this time shedding 43.25 % from its peak, real damage was"}, "2095": {"doc_id": "astro_962e5bb7", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. evel on 19th Oct 2000, this time shedding 43.25 % from its peak, real damage was made which took markets to bear phase. Stock Market Astrology - 140 - Astrological theory of business cycles BSE Sensex It became most discussed financial scam of that time and it was UTI US-64 bonds scam. Person involved in that scam was barred for lifetime from trading into markets, but he is still feared to be operating in markets with different fake identities, as per concerns raised by SEBI early this year."}, "2096": {"doc_id": "astro_b209274e", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. with different fake identities, as per concerns raised by SEBI early this year. Thus we can conclude that when Sani transits through a fiery Rasi and receive conjunction, trine or opposition aspect from Guru, is bad for economy and it is a strong indication for collapse. Over-optimism and period of economic boom cannot survive any further under this astrological combination taking place in heaven. It is my humble advice for investors to stay out of investment and remain sitting in cash during such an astrological combination. 'Cash is King' slogan holds true under this astrological influence."}, "2097": {"doc_id": "astro_c6a87802", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ombination. 'Cash is King' slogan holds true under this astrological influence. 2) Phase of recovery and revival This phase starts in economy when confident entrepreneurs start taking fresh risks and investment decisions in sectors they feel confident of making profits. Investors start investing in fundamentally stronger sectors and in stocks at rock bottom prices. Farmers start sowing in earth with confidence that this time they won't face huge losses, as was case in earlier phase. Prices of stocks at rock bottom levels attract fresh investors and fresh investments."}, "2098": {"doc_id": "astro_85a03573", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. of stocks at rock bottom levels attract fresh investors and fresh investments. Bottom fishing of stocks take place, at rock bottom price levels, by confident investors in fundamentally stronger sectors and stocks. This happens in recovery phase. This happens when Sani transits an earthy Rasi of zodiac, namely Vrisabha, Kanya and Makara, aspected by Guru. Remember that aspect of Guru is must for any major financial investments to take place."}, "2099": {"doc_id": "astro_d8f94720", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. that aspect of Guru is must for any major financial investments to take place. Thus conjunction, trine or opposition aspect of Guru at Sani transiting through an earthy Rasi of zodiac, leads to beginning of a new economic cycle through phase of economic recovery and revival. This phase is also good for starting any fresh economic venture, business, fresh investment and fresh launch of any enterprise. It is period of hard work at ground level or down-to-earth realistic level with an optimism, confidence and fresh energy for future gains."}, "2100": {"doc_id": "astro_45a727ee", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. realistic level with an optimism, confidence and fresh energy for future gains. Stock Market Astrology - 141 - Astrological theory of business cycles 3) Phase of growth and expansion At this phase investment made in previous phase starts growing, expanding and fetching good returns to investment. Profits start getting visible and are reinvested for further gains and higher returns. Diversification of investment also takes place during this phase. Investors start tapping untapped sectors and stocks, where higher risk is involved and which they left for investing in previous phase."}, "2101": {"doc_id": "astro_a5512e59", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. re higher risk is involved and which they left for investing in previous phase. Thus investment grows and expansion of economic activities takes place during this phase. This happens when Sani transits through an airy Rasi of zodiac, namely Mithuna, Tula and Kumbha, aspected by conjunction or trine of Guru. Sani in airy Rasi expands confidence, being in a friendly Rasi. It helps growth to spread from one sector to other. All economic chain starts functioning normally, growth and economic activities spread across all sectors of economy."}, "2102": {"doc_id": "astro_fadc34b0", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. normally, growth and economic activities spread across all sectors of economy. Thus this phase of economic activity enables returns to investments to get visible, and EPS (earnings per share) grows up. Companies start declaring good dividends and bonuses. They come up with expansion plans to participate in economic rally, like air expands across globe, with fear of being left out in growth rally or fear of missing away this rally of economic growth. 4) Phase of over-expansion and boom This phase is ripened phase of economic activity."}, "2103": {"doc_id": "astro_d7c3f492", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. se of over-expansion and boom This phase is ripened phase of economic activity. In other words, this is phase before burst out of ripened economic fruits takes place. This is phase when people start running blindly for profits and huge expansion of business activities takes place. Entrepreneurs desire to capture and tap entire market by over-employing manpower. Companies indulge into over-production and over-advertising, to catch vast and vast business empire for their product. Entrepreneurs start taking huge risks for unlimited profits, in over-confidence."}, "2104": {"doc_id": "astro_2462b1c4", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ntrepreneurs start taking huge risks for unlimited profits, in over-confidence. Investors start investing in any scrip, without looking into fundamental validity of scrip. Investors start making entry at over-brought price levels, with expectation of profits and due to fear of not getting left out of price rally in stock markets. Less confident investors too develop confidence and enter into investment, while confident investors turn into over-confident in this phase of economy."}, "2105": {"doc_id": "astro_e9842295", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. t, while confident investors turn into over-confident in this phase of economy. Blind buying and over-investment in stock markets become visible with abnormal rally in stock prices during this phase. Buying spree in market takes market to new heights, making regular fresh records of all time highs in stock prices and market indices. This phase of over-expansion and economic boom happens when Sani transits through a watery Rasi of zodiac, aspected by Guru. As water overflows and gets flooded everywhere, so does stock markets get flooded with investors and investments."}, "2106": {"doc_id": "astro_bcaebb2a", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. d everywhere, so does stock markets get flooded with investors and investments. Consumer markets get flooded with excessive products of Stock Market Astrology - 142 - Astrological theory of business cycles different brands and makes, resulting from over-production, over-investment and over-employment of manpower in economy. A flood of investment, employment and production gets visible during this phase of economic activity, which is an alarming signal for a clever investor to withdraw his profits and his investments from markets, by keeping aside further greed and sit with cash in hands."}, "2107": {"doc_id": "astro_d8015a78", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. tments from markets, by keeping aside further greed and sit with cash in hands. It is time to get ready with cash and be prepared for any fresh opportunity to invest at lower levels during next phase of economic recession or to enter at phase economic recovery. This is time to eat up ripened economic fruit, before it bursts out in next phase and fall down to ground in next phase of economic recession. But keeping aside greed becomes very difficult by entrepreneurs and investors, especially during this phase because more flood, more is thirst."}, "2108": {"doc_id": "astro_82efd08b", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. and investors, especially during this phase because more flood, more is thirst. Therefore they get indulged into over-investment and over-expansion, with motive of earning more and more profits and more and more returns to their investments. This period is marked by period of over-optimism, over-investment, over- employment, over-production, over-expansion and period of overall economic boom. 16.2 Historical evidences of major economic recessions? ? including Great depression of 1930 & Subprime mortgage crisis of 2008, confirming astrological theory of business cycles."}, "2109": {"doc_id": "astro_0813103d", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ime mortgage crisis of 2008, confirming astrological theory of business cycles. Periods of Planetary economic combinations recessions responsible 1921 Sani and Guru in Simha. 1930 Great Post Sani in Dhanur and Guru in Mithuna. War Depression 1940 Post War Sani and Guru in Mesha. Depression 1978 Sani in Simha and Guru in Mithuna. 1979 Sani and Guru in Simha. 1990 Sani in Dhanur and Guru in Mithuna. 2008 Sani in Simha and Guru in Dhanur."}, "2110": {"doc_id": "astro_fcb3108a", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. 1990 Sani in Dhanur and Guru in Mithuna. 2008 Sani in Simha and Guru in Dhanur. All above periods of economic recession satisfies conditions necessary for economic recession, as per astrological theory of business cycles, hence they confirm validity of above theory. Stock Market Astrology - 143 - Astrological analysis of gold 16.3 Watch out list of forthcoming combinations List of forthcoming recessionary combinations in coming 50 years, as per astrological theory of business cycles. 2017-18 Sani in Dhanur and Guru in Tula. 2028-29 Sani in Mesha and Guru in Simha and Tula."}, "2111": {"doc_id": "astro_54446080", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. i in Dhanur and Guru in Tula. 2028-29 Sani in Mesha and Guru in Simha and Tula. 2036-38 Sani in Simha and Guru in Mithuna. 2047-48 Sani in Dhanur and Guru in Mesha and Mithuna. 2058-59 Sani in Mesha and Guru in Mesha. Any of above 5 planetary combinations can prove to be worst ever recessionary period, for economic activities on this earth, in coming 50 years. Therefore it is my recommendation to astrologers and investors to book their profits ahead of these adverse planetary combinations to take place in heaven."}, "2112": {"doc_id": "astro_f384e2e0", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. profits ahead of these adverse planetary combinations to take place in heaven. Investors are advised to stay safe and trade cautiously with strict stop loss during these periods of adverse planetary combinations. Smart investors take note of each and every indicators of warning, whether it be a simple bad news, negative technical indicator or a fatal astrological combination. It is better to manage losses, than to ruining everything by blindly running after profits. No loss with small profits is better than huge profits with huge losses."}, "2113": {"doc_id": "astro_5ed4aaf7", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ofits. No loss with small profits is better than huge profits with huge losses. As it is wiser to sleep at night than during daytime, so it is wise to stay away from investments during adverse or recessionary periods. Remember, recession is economic night and boom is economic evening, so wake up early in morning, go for your work, work during day and return back to your home with evening, before night, because night is meant for sleeping and recharging with energy for next days activity."}, "2114": {"doc_id": "astro_00514d7d", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. night is meant for sleeping and recharging with energy for next days activity. Chapter 17 Astrological analysis of gold price cycles Gold, most beautiful of all precious metals, has a symbol of glory involved with it. Person possessing it feels confident, beautified, dignified and glorified. It has been so because influence of Guru is attached to it and a person who may posses this metal to a greatest extent, is believed to attract qualities and influences of Guru to greatest extent, hence his or her getting dignified, glorified, beautified, graceful appearance, confident, successful, wealthy"}, "2115": {"doc_id": "astro_43d4c94f", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. fied, glorified, beautified, graceful appearance, confident, successful, wealthy and lucky becomes a common phenomenon. Stock Market Astrology - 144 - Astrological analysis of gold Ever since ages of civilization, gold was most preferred of all precious metals for investment, not only among metals, but earlier it was only preferred kind of investment. In India it was also attached to mythology and is considered auspicious to posses in home as ornaments. Women like ornaments made of gold most."}, "2116": {"doc_id": "astro_db945613", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. picious to posses in home as ornaments. Women like ornaments made of gold most. Indian women are deeply attached to gold and gold ornaments, it is believed auspicious to wear at all auspicious occasions. Wearing gold over body invites blessing from Deva Guru Brihaspati, Guru within body, mind and soul. Gold - 1983 to Aug 2009 Therefore gold prices are also directly attached to strength and weakness of Guru, while in transit through various Rasis of zodiac and kind of aspect it receives from other Grahas."}, "2117": {"doc_id": "astro_14030f8f", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. rough various Rasis of zodiac and kind of aspect it receives from other Grahas. Guru remains strong while in transit through ruling, exalted or a friendly Rasi, or receiving favorable aspect from other Grahas, so does price of gold remain strong in markets. While in transit through an enemy or a Rasi of fall [debilitation], or aspected by malefic Grahas, Guru remain weak and so does price of gold in market slip down. As long Guru remains udita [rising] in horizon, demand for gold rises up and prices also rise up in market."}, "2118": {"doc_id": "astro_7ec506ff", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. rising] in horizon, demand for gold rises up and prices also rise up in market. Whereas during period when Guru remain asta [setting] in horizon, demand for gold falls down and price of gold also get adversely effected. Stock Market Astrology - 145 - Astrological analysis of gold Gold meets hyper inflation with depression in stock markets, but this metal too shines in its prices with cycle of Guru in heaven. Every times Guru gains strength in heaven, gold starts shining more brightly, attracting investor or buyer interest into it, so does it reflect in its price movements too."}, "2119": {"doc_id": "astro_8da388b4", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. estor or buyer interest into it, so does it reflect in its price movements too. Thus shine of this yellow metal is fully dependent on cycle of Guru in heaven. 10-year gold chart in USD Guru, aspected by Surya or Chandr, is always favorable for this precious metal and gold prices gain strength during this aspect. Guru aspected by Rahu and Ketu is also good for gold prices, as it brings a period of hyperinflation in gold prices and prices of gold surge up dramatically during this aspect."}, "2120": {"doc_id": "astro_bb3f4616", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ion in gold prices and prices of gold surge up dramatically during this aspect. Above mentioned planetary combinations took place in 2008, when Guru and Rahu came near to each other within 30?, during May and Jun 2008, and gold prices were trading between US $ 900 ? US $ 1000 an ounce, then but it reached US $ 1000 per ounce mark, in Mar 2008, with Grahas approaching to each other, but it fell down to US $ 700 an ounce level in Nov 2008, as Guru became retrograde and separated away from Rahu, from Jun to Sep 2008."}, "2121": {"doc_id": "astro_c6980964", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. , as Guru became retrograde and separated away from Rahu, from Jun to Sep 2008. Again when Guru became direct and both Rahu and Guru neared in for a conjunction, gold started rising in its strength and again touched US $ 1000 per ounce mark, with exact conjunction during Feb 2009. And this time it is expected to remain stronger and touch new highs till end of 2009, until these two Grahas get separated away from each other, with Guru moving out of Makara to Kumbha, and Rahu moving out of Makara to Dhanur, during end of Dec 2009."}, "2122": {"doc_id": "astro_fa1cbc83", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ara to Kumbha, and Rahu moving out of Makara to Dhanur, during end of Dec 2009. Meanwhile, during process of publication of this book gold, prices Stock Market Astrology - 146 - Astrological analysis of gold crossed $ 1150 level in Nov 2009, and is expected to reach $ 1200 per ounce by end of Dec 2009. Guru cycles are related to gold cycles. It is well known that Guru rules gold - \"Gurum Kachana Sannibham\", as used to be said by our ancient sages."}, "2123": {"doc_id": "astro_cfafc3e7", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ules gold - \"Gurum Kachana Sannibham\", as used to be said by our ancient sages. Based on transits of Guru, gold's boom and recession can be predicted, if carefully studied about all its transits, especially conjunctions of Guru with Rahu or Ketu, which brings hyperinflation to this metal and its price surges up as never before, with this planetary aspect. Gold - Jan 2007 to Aug 2009 Stock Market Astrology - 147 - Astrological analysis of gold Gold - 1983 to Aug 2009 Historical evidences of Guru - Rahu / Ketu conjunction in gold prices 1) Year 1781 was hyper inflationary for gold."}, "2124": {"doc_id": "astro_76c98ca8", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. / Ketu conjunction in gold prices 1) Year 1781 was hyper inflationary for gold. American revolutionary war rendered continental currency valueless. On 31st May 1781, gold price soared to $ 19,390 an ounce, with Guru in conjunction with Rahu. 2) In 1837, because of financial panic and hyperinflation in gold price, with huge demand for this metal came up, to meet crisis, U.S. government suspended free gold conversion. This time Guru was seen in conjunction with Ketu in Kanya during 1838. 3) In 1893, another financial panic occurred and gold was hoarded."}, "2125": {"doc_id": "astro_8e34b5ed", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. during 1838. 3) In 1893, another financial panic occurred and gold was hoarded. In Oct 1893, discount rate soared to 36 %. This time Guru was seen in conjunction with Rahu in Mesha, during 1893. 4) In 1948, again gold prices soared up, with transiting Guru in conjunction with Ketu in Vrisabha. 5) Period from early Sep 1979 through end of Jun 1980 was extremely bullish for gold, with Guru forming a conjunction aspect with Rahu in Simha. Spot gold was then quoted at US $ 370 an ounce in early Nov 1979. It soared to US $ 875 on 21st Jan 1980."}, "2126": {"doc_id": "astro_41dc2e65", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. at US $ 370 an ounce in early Nov 1979. It soared to US $ 875 on 21st Jan 1980. There was a sharp downward reaction in Feb and Mar 1980, touching a low of US $ 475. Gold then climbed all way up during rest of bullish phase. Its price overshot past level by end of Jun 1980, reaching US $ 690 in early Jul. Stock Market Astrology - 148 - Astrological analysis of crude oil 6) From Feb 1987 to Feb 1987 [? original text], Guru was in conjunction with Rahu in Mina, as a result of it gold prices again soared to US $ 500 an ounce from US $ 350 an ounce."}, "2127": {"doc_id": "astro_7be16d36", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ult of it gold prices again soared to US $ 500 an ounce from US $ 350 an ounce. Chapter 18 Astrologicalanalysis of crude oil price cycles Crude oil is also known as black gold, because of scarcity and high prices quoted for it. As people love to invest and store gold in maximum quantities, so do nations and states love to acquire and store crude for their prosperity and smooth functioning of nation, by defying any situation of crisis in crude oil within their country."}, "2128": {"doc_id": "astro_eef3b48e", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. f nation, by defying any situation of crisis in crude oil within their country. U.S., China, India and many other countries of world indulge into building up of buffer stocks of crude within their country, apart from storage of regular quantity in demand, to meet any situation of crude oil crisis. All nations know that any crisis in crude oil can take economy of any nation for a nose dive. Gulf countries and other crude abundant or crude producing nations are enjoying glory due to their possession of crude."}, "2129": {"doc_id": "astro_84472159", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. or crude producing nations are enjoying glory due to their possession of crude. Their economy is completely dependent on crude and day by day flourishing to new glories only due to their possession of crude. These days crude play a major role in any national economy as well as in global economy. Prices of crude may lead an economy to glory or gloom. Any sharp rise in crude oil price may bring glory to crude producing nations, but it will lead economy of crude consuming nations to gloom."}, "2130": {"doc_id": "astro_b3c372f6", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. roducing nations, but it will lead economy of crude consuming nations to gloom. Whereas, any sharp fall in crude oil prices will create glory for economies of crude consuming nations and gloom to economies of crude producing nations. Therefore, analysis of crude oil prices has become need of time due to its important position in any modern economy, especially oil economies of world. Traders across globe also love most to trade in crude and earn profits with their speculations in crude oil prices."}, "2131": {"doc_id": "astro_742cae78", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. to trade in crude and earn profits with their speculations in crude oil prices. Astrologically, crude is influenced by many Grahas, like Chandr, Sani, Uranus, Neptune, Rahu and Ketu, and mutual aspects between them. Whenever these Grahas get beneficially positioned in zodiac or aspected by benefics, crude prices soar up, especially with conjunction of Sani with Rahu or Ketu. Whenever Rahu or Ketu form conjunction aspect to Sani, crude prices soar up, and whenever these Grahas get separated from conjunction with Sani, crude prices plunge down from its peak."}, "2132": {"doc_id": "astro_6899f6eb", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. t separated from conjunction with Sani, crude prices plunge down from its peak. Stock Market Astrology - 149 - Astrological analysis of crude oil Crude oil - Jan 2004 to Oct 2009 Historical evidences of Sani - Rahu / Ketu conjunction in crude oil prices 1) In Jul 2008, crude touched high of US $ 147 a barrel, after starting to soar up in prices from Jul 2007. Sani in Simha, in conjunction with Ketu, from Jul 2007, kept this volatile fluid bubbling hot till Jul 2008."}, "2133": {"doc_id": "astro_376db29e", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. with Ketu, from Jul 2007, kept this volatile fluid bubbling hot till Jul 2008. Even with Ketu changing Rasi in May 2008, this volatile fluid was kept hot and bubbling till Jul 2008, Ketu still being within cusp of Rasi, until it touched all time high of US $ 147 a barrel in Jul 2008. Finally, this black gold lost all its bubble with Ketu moving away from conjunction with Sani in Simha, and soon it touched low of US $ 32 per barrel in Jan 2009, shedding US $ 115 from its peak level, within a short span of few months period."}, "2134": {"doc_id": "astro_9611a65f", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. hedding US $ 115 from its peak level, within a short span of few months period. It happened so because Ketu moved to a watery Rasi Karkataka, to get itself cooled from burning heat of previous Rasi Simha, which was burning hot due to its fiery nature. 2) From Mar 2002 to Mar 2003, Sani was in Vrisabha and was in conjunction with Rahu, crude oil soared from below US $ 20 a barrel to US $ 38 a barrel. After separation of this conjunction, crude soon plunged to low of US $ 26 a barrel in Apr 2003."}, "2135": {"doc_id": "astro_c594ffb7", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. of this conjunction, crude soon plunged to low of US $ 26 a barrel in Apr 2003. Stock Market Astrology - 150 - Diwali Muhrat trading Forthcoming combination From Jan 2013 to Jul 2014, Sani will be transiting through Tula, in conjunction with Rahu. At that time crude is expected to soar up in its price and it is expected to cross US $ 250 per barrel mark, and trade within US $ 250 to US $ 350 levels, before plunge with separation of said conjunction. Chapter 19 Diwali Muhrat trading - annual trend indicator for stock markets Muhrat trading on Diwali day has special significance in India."}, "2136": {"doc_id": "astro_7814964c", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. r stock markets Muhrat trading on Diwali day has special significance in India. It is considered as auspicious among trading community, to begin trading with beginning of new Samvat on this day, for happy and profitable trading throughout year. Traders consider it auspicious to buy shares during Muhrat trading with beginning of new Samvat or new business year. It is a symbolic ritual which has been performed for years and years in our country. Muhrat trading in stock market happens for about an hour on every Diwali day. Usually, this one hour trading session is held in evening."}, "2137": {"doc_id": "astro_66f0abd1", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. on every Diwali day. Usually, this one hour trading session is held in evening. It is considered a good omen for markets, if Muhrat trading closes with gains in a positive territory, and year ahead is likely to be positive for markets. Whereas, if Muhrat trading closes with loss in a negative territory, then its considered a bad omen for markets and year ahead is supposed to bring gloom and darkness in markets."}, "2138": {"doc_id": "astro_605cef46", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. for markets and year ahead is supposed to bring gloom and darkness in markets. People believe that if bulls dominate Muhrat trading then bulls will be able to dominate markets for entire Samvat year, and markets will reach to new heights, but if bears become able to dominate Muhrat trading session, then bears will be dominating over markets for entire Samvat year, and markets will plunge down and bring gloom to investors. History also confirms to above belief among traders, and Muhrat trading has become an important trend indicator for stock markets."}, "2139": {"doc_id": "astro_d6523227", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. , and Muhrat trading has become an important trend indicator for stock markets. Traditional traders in market don't take this indicator lightly, and pay a great deal of importance to it, at least in our country India. I remember that before Jan 2008, actual collapse of stock markets and Subprime mortgage crisis coming into news, its shadow has been cast well before actual event in Diwali Muhrat trading day of 9th Nov 2007, when markets pared 151 points, to close into negative territory on Muhrat trading day, for first time in past seven years."}, "2140": {"doc_id": "astro_19dbd4cf", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. o negative territory on Muhrat trading day, for first time in past seven years. An alarm was raised, experienced traders were worried, but there was no one to believe them, until Jan 2008 came, with all panic and gloom in markets. Stock Market Astrology - 151 - Study of correlation By time 28th Oct 2008 Diwali day approached, investors and traders world over were engulfed by fear of worst ever recession, there was panic and gloom everywhere, after Jan 2008 crash and Sep 2008 nose dive in markets."}, "2141": {"doc_id": "astro_88c0beb0", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. c and gloom everywhere, after Jan 2008 crash and Sep 2008 nose dive in markets. No one believed that this time Muhrat trading will be able to close with positive gains and fear was all around market. Diwali day of 28th Oct 2008 came in and Diwali Muhrat trading began, but results were dramatic, beyond anybody's expectation. Benchmark index surged 498 points to close above 9K at end of one-hour Muhrat session, to mark beginning of Samvat 2065. Sensex closed at 9,034, gaining 499 points, while broader Nifty ended at 2,684, up 160 points."}, "2142": {"doc_id": "astro_9e8a3ff7", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. t 9,034, gaining 499 points, while broader Nifty ended at 2,684, up 160 points. Indication was positive for markets ahead, and recovery from lows was now for sure shot. And we all know how markets made non-stop journey of recovery after that, and crossed over 17K mark before Diwali 2009, from bottom level of 9K of Diwali 2008. Hence, it is impossible to deny that Diwali Muhrat trading is of great importance as an indicator, to predetermine and understand future trend of market."}, "2143": {"doc_id": "astro_b0f8118d", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ortance as an indicator, to predetermine and understand future trend of market. Traders and investors may simply look for its positive or negative closing to plan their short term investment in markets, for next one year. If all astrological factors taken together, along with indications of Muhrat trading, investor or trader can reach into a smart investment decision, for his or her benefit and can make handsome profits out of swinging markets."}, "2144": {"doc_id": "astro_5fe85cbf", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. , for his or her benefit and can make handsome profits out of swinging markets. Chapter 20 Study of correlation between stock markets and gold prices Stock markets and gold prices have partial correlation between them, but this partial correlation plays an important role for those who love to churn their investments or portfolio from stocks to gold and gold to stocks, by looking into opportunities for handsome returns to their investments."}, "2145": {"doc_id": "astro_60870207", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. tocks, by looking into opportunities for handsome returns to their investments. Partial correlation between stock markets and gold prices is that whenever stock markets collapse from its peak, then gold prices meet hyperinflation and start rising up abnormally. This happens so because investors start withdrawing their money from stock markets, invest them into gold in search of a safe heaven for their investments."}, "2146": {"doc_id": "astro_e6c8fcb0", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. arkets, invest them into gold in search of a safe heaven for their investments. Smart traders foresees these opportunities and start churning their portfolios from stocks to gold ahead of others to capture these investor sentiments and get it converted into handsome profits for themselves. Whenever stock markets start showing a bull run and start to reach its peak with stock Stock Market Astrology - 152 - Study of correlation markets boom, a smart investor start booking profits in small quantities with every rise in stock markets and start shifting their investment to gold."}, "2147": {"doc_id": "astro_0c659203", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. s with every rise in stock markets and start shifting their investment to gold. And withdraws all his investment with first remarkable fall in stock markets and shift almost all his investment into gold, before bears grab stock markets into their claws and all other people withdraw their investments from stock markets and get into investing in gold. Thus he enters into gold ahead of others and when all others jump into it, he starts booking his profits in gold with rising demand of gold and its rising prices, that too ahead of others."}, "2148": {"doc_id": "astro_74c3ee22", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. old with rising demand of gold and its rising prices, that too ahead of others. Here one must remember that sooner stock markets start recovering from lows, gold prices start slipping with investors resorting to book profits in gold and shifting their investments to stock markets again, with value buying of stocks at rock bottom levels of their prices."}, "2149": {"doc_id": "astro_9a7ced50", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. rkets again, with value buying of stocks at rock bottom levels of their prices. A smart investor or trader need to learn all these phenomenon of investor sentiments and utilize them, along with their astrological findings for making their investment decisions into right stock at a right time, in order to earn maximum profits to their investment or into their portfolio from financial markets at an earliest possible time. Stock markets and gold prices are cyclical in nature, every upside is followed by a down swing and every down swing is followed by an up swing."}, "2150": {"doc_id": "astro_09f1b908", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. de is followed by a down swing and every down swing is followed by an up swing. Grabbing right opportunity at right time is key to success in these financial markets. Buying at bottom and selling at peak and vice versa, fetches profits in these markets. Although it's practically impossible to catch exact bottom and exact peak of markets, but it's not difficult to pick near bottom and near peak levels with help of astrological insight, and convert them into profitable trading."}, "2151": {"doc_id": "astro_9907042d", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ls with help of astrological insight, and convert them into profitable trading. HARI OM TAT SAT Stock Market Astrology - 153 - Study of correlation About the book \"Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles\" is first ever systematic work on astrological influences on stock markets and stock prices, based on 11 years of aggressive research, carried out with wisdom gained through 20 years of professional experience in field of astrology."}, "2152": {"doc_id": "astro_80a38d45", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. isdom gained through 20 years of professional experience in field of astrology. There has been a persistent demand for some dependable method of predicting stock markets with greater accuracy, and this book will hopefully fill that gap successfully. Language of book is simple and complex astrological principles were also explained in a very simple manner that anyone, with little knowledge of astrology, can easily grasp these principles to predict business cycles, periods of economic recession, panic and direction of stock prices successfully and use them accordingly for trading in stock market"}, "2153": {"doc_id": "astro_4b631c00", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. f stock prices successfully and use them accordingly for trading in stock markets. Fundamental idea behind this book was that stock markets are governed by investor sentiments of greed and fear, and fact remains true that all human sentiments, whether sentiment of greed or fear, are governed by astrological influences on human brains, which drives brain to take any buying or selling decision in markets. This book explains implications of all planetary transits through 12 Rasis of zodiac in chapter 'TRANSIT OF PLANETS THROUGH TWELVE SIGNS OF ZODIAC'."}, "2154": {"doc_id": "astro_e7c2272d", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. Rasis of zodiac in chapter 'TRANSIT OF PLANETS THROUGH TWELVE SIGNS OF ZODIAC'. Implications of transit of Chandr through each of 27 Nakshatras are explained with real examples of intraday trading, in chapter 'PRACTICAL INTRADAY TRADING WITH TRANSIT OF MOON THROUGH 27 NAKSHATRAS'. Influence of any particular Graha gets intensified during certain particular hours of a day, which is known as Hora. Formulating trading strategies in intraday with help of Hora is explained, with real examples of intraday trading, in chapter 'PRACTICAL STRATEGIES OF INTRADAY TRADING WITH HORA - PLANETARY HOURS'."}, "2155": {"doc_id": "astro_8bfab084", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. chapter 'PRACTICAL STRATEGIES OF INTRADAY TRADING WITH HORA - PLANETARY HOURS'. An additional method for timing price movements is also explained in book, with help of micro projection of Vimshottari Dasha system. Intraday, short term and long term price movement in stock prices for 30 different sectors of market is explained in chapter 'SECTOR-WISE PREDICTING INTRADAY, SHORT & LONG TERM MARKET OUTLOOK'. Chapter 'ASTROLOGICAL ANALYSIS OF GOLD PRICE CYCLES' explains principle for determining movements in gold prices."}, "2156": {"doc_id": "astro_23969300", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. GOLD PRICE CYCLES' explains principle for determining movements in gold prices. And chapter 'ASTROLOGICAL ANALYSIS OF CRUDE OIL PRICE CYCLES' explains about principle for determining movements in crude oil prices. Stock markets are often influenced by business cycles and it has been a challenge for a long time to successfully predict occurrence of any business cycle in advance. For first time, relationship between astrological phenomenon and business cycles has been successfully established, which is thoroughly explained in chapter 'ASTROLOGICAL THEORY OF BUSINESS CYCLES'."}, "2157": {"doc_id": "astro_0ddbd8aa", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. ch is thoroughly explained in chapter 'ASTROLOGICAL THEORY OF BUSINESS CYCLES'. Stock Market Astrology - 154 - Study of correlation Authenticity of this principle has been established with help of historical evidences, discussed in chapter 'HISTORICAL EVIDENCES OF MAJOR ECONOMIC RECESSIONS'. Prediction for forthcoming periods of economic recessions has also been made for help of readers, in chapter 'WATCH OUT LIST OF FORTHCOMING COMBINATIONS'. This book also explains principle of sunspot theory of business cycle, in chapter 'SUNSPOT THEORY OF BUSINESS CYCLE'."}, "2158": {"doc_id": "astro_f44d319f", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. unspot theory of business cycle, in chapter 'SUNSPOT THEORY OF BUSINESS CYCLE'. Various other astrological periodicities, helpful in determining business cycles, were also discussed in chapter 'ASTROLOGICAL PERIODICITIES IN BUSINESS CYCLES'. Many such useful astrological principles has been thoroughly discussed in book, which makes this book very useful for investors, traders and analysts of stock markets, as well as for any astrologer seriously interested in predicting stock markets. Re-edited by Chistabo. All efforts have been made to reproduce this publication in original form."}, "2159": {"doc_id": "astro_b63be587", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stock Market Astrology & Astrological Theory of Business Cycles (Indrodeep Banerjee, 2009). Topic: Indian/Vedic system, NSE sector-planet mapping, Nakshatras, Hora trading. abo. All efforts have been made to reproduce this publication in original form. Though, I have allowed myself regular (to me) modifications - all Grahas names are in Hindi (actually Tamil). May the Light shine on all of us, Simon Ashtami Krishna Paksha, Bhadrapada Masa, Nandana Varsha (2012)."}, "2160": {"doc_id": "astro_0a8bd75d", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stellar Theology and Masonic Astronomy (Robert Hewitt Brown, 1882). Topic: stellar symbolism, ancient astronomy, zodiac history. ONTENTS Forward Understanding Why This Book is Important by Jordan Maxwell: ...........................vii Part First Chapter 1 Introduction ? A Few Words to the Masonic Fraternity................................................. 2 Chapter 2 The Ancient Mysteries Described ....................... 6 Chapter 3 A Chapter of Astronomical Facts...........................41 The Ecliptic.............................................................."}, "2161": {"doc_id": "astro_3b2e826e", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stellar Theology and Masonic Astronomy (Robert Hewitt Brown, 1882). Topic: stellar symbolism, ancient astronomy, zodiac history. ..41 The Ecliptic.............................................................. 42 The Zodiac...............................................................42 Aries.........................................................................43 Taurus.......................................................................43 Gemini ...................................................................44 Cancer......................................................................44 Leo ..........................................................................45 Virgo......................................"}, "2162": {"doc_id": "astro_6ac33850", "domain": "ASTRO", "text": "[AstroFinance Knowledge] Stellar Theology and Masonic Astronomy (Robert Hewitt Brown, 1882). Topic: stellar symbolism, ancient astronomy, zodiac history. ..................................45 Virgo.............................